access_log stderr, as error_log has it

A service on Dukovo writes its log to its standard error output, which
Spark copies into the system's log (logd(8)), where logtrim(8) trims it and
log(1) reads it by service. error_log takes "stderr" for that; this
lets access_log take it too, rather than a file of that name.

diff --git a/src/http/modules/ngx_http_log_module.c b/src/http/modules/ngx_http_log_module.c
index 9158974..bbbaa14 100644
--- a/src/http/modules/ngx_http_log_module.c
+++ b/src/http/modules/ngx_http_log_module.c
@@ -1413,6 +1413,23 @@ ngx_http_log_set_log(ngx_conf_t *cf, ngx_command_t *cmd, void *conf)
         goto process_formats;
     }
 
+    if (ngx_strcmp(value[1].data, "stderr") == 0) {
+
+        /*
+         * The standard error output, as error_log has it (Dukovo's patch):
+         * a service's, which the system's log keeps.
+         */
+
+        ngx_str_null(&s);
+
+        log->file = ngx_conf_open_file(cf->cycle, &s);
+        if (log->file == NULL) {
+            return NGX_CONF_ERROR;
+        }
+
+        goto process_formats;
+    }
+
     n = ngx_http_script_variables_count(&value[1]);
 
     if (n == 0) {
